Strides equal to the C-contiguous strides for an array's shape are ignored, and
are no longer written out (previously strides were incorrectly treated as being
in units of elements rather than bytes when deciding whether to write them).

Strided arrays written with inline storage are written in C order.

Also fixed a bug where ndarray datatype conversions did not properly accumulate
the overflow flag across rows; that is, overflow was only reported if it
occurred on the last row when reading an (N > 1)-D tile.
